  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Vent Invertebrates Collected at Gorda Ridge",
  "description": "The Field Museum's Vent Invertebrates Collection Database provides data on specimens collected at Gorda Ridge by Janet R. Voight during the 2002 cruise. Cruise details are as follows: R/V Western Flyer with the Remote Vehicle Tiburon, partially funded by NURP Grants POFP005001/AK-99-13 and PO FP206164/CA-02-04 to Zierenberg and McClain UC Davis and by the Monterey Bay Aquarium Research Institute (MBARI). Vent Fields: Escanaba Trough and GR-14.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To give potential users of our collection advance information about material available by loan or for on-site study.",
